KZ3 patch 2148 (RSX pass 138): LD_CB_REUSE, reuse the previous draw's vertex constant-buffer slot. Default off.

Every live draw copies the 512 transform constants plus an 8-float tail (viewport transform) into a slot of the constant
ring (8 KB of write-combined memory per draw). With LD_CB_REUSE=1 a draw whose constants are unchanged since the draw that
filled the previous slot, and whose tail bytes are equal, points its root CBV at that slot and skips the copy; the ring
does not advance for it. "Unchanged" is a generation counter (rsx_dispatch.const_gen) bumped by every writer of the
stored constants when a value changes: the transform-constant upload in rsx_dispatch.c, the constant seed, and the camera
repair in rsx_live_draw.c. The previous slot must also lie below the ring's write position, and every ring reset
invalidates it. The decision is in rsx_cb_reuse.h (pure functions) and is tested by tools/smoke/test_ld_cb_reuse.sh.

With RSX_PERF=1 the [perf-walk] line ends with "| cbv copy N reuse M": draws that copied vs reused the slot.


